{"id":"n50077725d1","headline":"Greek Tax Burden Outpaced Income Growth by 10 Points Due to Fiscal Drag","summary":"New data shows household earnings growth lagged the rise in tax burden in Greece, widening the gap between incomes and purchasing power. The article attributes this to shifting fiscal policy.","why":"Fiscal drag occurs when inflation and wage growth push households into higher tax brackets, reducing disposable income and consumer spending. Greece's fiscal position matters to euro-area bond and equity investors.","category":"economy","event_type":"macro-data","importance":1,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Athens","country":"Greece","lat":37.98,"lon":23.73,"region":"eu"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"PravdaReport","url":"https://english.pravda.ru/news/world/173134-greece-tax-burden-analysis/"},"sources":[{"name":"PravdaReport","url":"https://english.pravda.ru/news/world/173134-greece-tax-burden-analysis/"}],"published_at":"2026-11-17T06:14:00Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-17T08:41:28Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"449a7fccf1b669cb","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-17T08:41:28Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-11-17T06:14:00Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-11-17T08:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"GR","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/banknotes-money-7881948.jpg","alt":"banknotes money (illustration)","credit":"Barta4","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/money-cash-dollars-finance-7881948/"}}